  - Key: window:GameObject
    Title: Prefab Object
    Summary: One of this prefab's objects. Behaviors attach to it; drag it into the graph to refer to it.
    Description: 
  - Key: window:GameView
    Title: The Game View
    Summary: What the player sees through the game's camera. Press Play to run the game here.
    Description: 
  - Key: window:InspectorWindow
    Title: The Inspector
    Summary: The settings of whatever is selected. Select something and drop me here, and I'll tell you about it.
    Description: 
  - Key: window:ProjectBrowser
    Title: The Project Window
    Summary: 'All of the project''s files: prefabs, graphs, scripts, art. Select one and drop me here to hear about it.'
    Description: 
  - Key: window:SceneHierarchyWindow
    Title: The Hierarchy
    Summary: Every object in the open scenes, as a tree (children under their parents). Select one and drop me here to hear about it.
    Description: 
  - Key: window:SceneView
    Title: The Scene View
    Summary: Your level. Drop me on an object here and I'll tell you what it is and which Behaviors it has. In Prefab Mode, it shows the prefab you're editing.
    Description: 
  - Key: window:SchematicGraphEditorWindow
    Title: The Schematic Graph
    Summary: "Where an object's logic lives. Events (On Start, On Signal Received\u2026) start flows that run through action nodes along the arrows. The IO Dock on the left lists the prefab's objects with their Behaviors, Variables and Signals; drag any of them in to use them."
    Description: 
